brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net try to take a stab at this in your own implementation, try to find posts over the fire hose that are most similar to my last 100 posts at any given time using the methodology discussed above

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@fromthewestmeadow.com: If you can see this without following me you are in The West Meadow cluster
  [video, no alt text]
@ecombs1950.bsky.social: how about an explanation of the post?
@fromthewestmeadow.com: The visualization clusters posts by semantic similarity: PCA reduces high-dimensional text embeddings to 3D, so posts with similar content appear close together, forming natural clusters that reveal topic or style groupings among my posts and my mutuals’ posts.
@fromthewestmeadow.com: If you’re seeing this post, it’s because the algorithm identified that your post’s content is close to mine in this reduced, clustered space.
